hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1597","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah Al-Hashimi, He said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has He disobeys God, and whoever obeys the prince has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the prince has disobeyed me. The imam is only a shield, so if he prays sitting, then pray sitting, and if He said: God hears those who praise Him, so say: O God, our Lord, praise be to You. So if the words of the people of earth agree with the words of the people of heaven, he will be forgiven for what he said. He has passed away from his sin, and Chosroes will perish, and there will be no Chosroes after him, and Caesar will perish, and there will be no Caesar after him.”"
